      "mergeID": "651e8f410687ac0954a5f7fc",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Every person I have met that is using the Android Alpha has crackling audio coming from their microphone. This includes team members.\n\nIt appears to be the client not keeping up with reading/compressing/transmitting the audio. It is dropped samples, not compression quality issues. Definitely related to CPU load.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Microphone Audio Crackles when performance isn’t optimal",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64dedbaa76289b0999ef2e06",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yeah I have this issue too. When I have 20FPS people can understand me a bit, but starting from 15FPS I'm not understandable. \n\nThis bug is a deal breaker for me, and pretty sure for everyone using the Android version.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
